      "problem": "Express $\\log_3\\left(\\dfrac{2}{5}\\right)$ as a difference of logarithms.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\log_n(a) - \\log_n(b) = \\log_n\\left( \\dfrac{a}{b} \\right)\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule for logarithms, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{2}{5}) & ={log}_{3}⁡(2)-{log}_{3}⁡(5).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
